  ($q$alg-364$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation 9x + 5y = −3 is equivalent to y = mx + k, where m and k are constants. What is the value of m?$q$, $q$["9/5","−9/5","5/9","−5/9"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Solving for y: 5y = −9x − 3, so y = (−9/5)x − 3/5. Thus m = −9/5.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-365$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation A = p(q + 5r) relates the quantities A, p, q, and r. Which equation correctly gives r in terms of A, p, and q?$q$, $q$["r = (A + pq)/(5p)","r = 5p(A − q)","r = (A − pq)/(5p)","r = (A − pq)/5"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Divide both sides by p: A/p = q + 5r. Subtract q: A/p − q = 5r. Divide by 5: r = (A − pq)/(5p), after combining over a common denominator.$q$, null),
