  ($q$alg-533$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$The system of equations 2x + 5y = 3 and kx + 15y = 9 has infinitely many solutions. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["2","7","3","6"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Infinitely many solutions require the second equation to be a multiple of the first. Multiplying by 3 gives 6x + 15y = 9, so k = 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-534$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$The system of equations 4x + 4y = 8 and kx + 16y = 32 has infinitely many solutions. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["16","32","17","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Infinitely many solutions require the second equation to be a multiple of the first. Multiplying by 4 gives 16x + 16y = 32, so k = 16.$q$, null),
