  ($q$alg-640$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the largest integer value of x that satisfies −6x + 32 ≥ −6?$q$, $q$["7","−6","6","5"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$−6x ≥ −38. Dividing by −6 reverses the inequality: x ≤ 6.333. The largest integer is 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-641$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f is linear. If f(2) = 15 and f(6) = 35, what is the value of f(4)?$q$, $q$["15","30","20","25"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope is (35 − 15)/(6 − 2) = 5, and f(0) = 5. So f(4) = 5(4) + 5 = 25.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-642$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$A student has at most $42 to spend on notebooks and pens. Notebooks cost $3 each and pens cost $2 each. If the student buys 4 notebooks, what is the maximum number of pens the student can buy?$q$, $q$["21","14","16","15"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$3(4) + 2p ≤ 42 → 2p ≤ 30 → p ≤ 15. The maximum whole number is 15.$q$, null),
