  ($q$alg-645$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$A ticket office sold 70 regular and large tickets for a bakery in one day. Regular tickets cost $12 each, and large tickets cost $4 each. If the total revenue was $464, how many regular tickets were sold?$q$, $q$["23","18","60","28"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Let a be the number of regular tickets. Then a + s = 70 and 12a + 4s = 464. Substituting s = 70 − a gives 8a = 184, so a = 23.$q$, null),
