  ($q$alg-654$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A line has slope 4 and passes through the point (−2, 4). At what x-value does the line cross the x-axis?$q$, $q$["−3","−2","3","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$y = 4(x − (−2)) + 4. Setting y = 0 gives x − (−2) = −1, so x = −3.$q$, null),
