  ($q$alg-656$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 1, null, $q$A tank contains 430 gallons of water and drains at a constant rate of 8 gallons per minute. After how many minutes will the tank contain 246 gallons?$q$, $q$["21","184","23","28"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$430 − 8t = 246 → 8t = 184 → t = 23.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-657$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$A ticket office sold 92 adult and child tickets for a museum in one day. Adult tickets cost $10 each, and child tickets cost $7 each. If the total revenue was $785, how many adult tickets were sold?$q$, $q$["47","82","42","52"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Let a be the number of adult tickets. Then a + s = 92 and 10a + 7s = 785. Substituting s = 92 − a gives 3a = 141, so a = 47.$q$, null),
