  ($q$alg-661$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 1, null, $q$What is the slope of the line with equation −4x + 4y = 20?$q$, $q$["−4","4","−1","1"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Solve for y: y = 4/4 x + constant, so the slope is 1.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-662$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 1, null, $q$A climbing gym charges an equipment fee of $25 plus $25 per visit. A customer has paid a total of $475. How many visits has the customer paid for?$q$, $q$["450","18","20","19"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Let n be the number of visits. Then 25 + 25n = 475, so 25n = 450 and n = 18.$q$, null),
