  ($q$alg-666$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$y = 3x − 3<br>2x + 4y = 16<br><br>If (x, y) is the solution to the system of equations above, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["3","−2","14","2"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Substitute y = 3x − 3 into the second equation: 2x + 4(3x − 3) = 16, which simplifies to 14x − 12 = 16. So x = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-667$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$Which point (x, y) is a solution to the inequality y ≤ −2x − 3?$q$, $q$["(−2, 4)","(0, −6)","(−2, 5)","(0, −2)"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Substitute each point. For (0, −6): −2(0) − 3 = −3, and −6 ≤ −3 is true. Each other point makes the inequality false.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-668$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$Line ℓ in the xy-plane has slope −3 and passes through the point (−4, −1). Which of the following points also lies on line ℓ?$q$, $q$["(−6, 5)","(5, −6)","(−6, −7)","(−6, −1/3)"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Moving from x = −4 to x = −6 changes x by −2, so y changes by −3 × −2 = 6. The new y-value is −1 + 6 = 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-669$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$Line k is perpendicular to the line with equation −4x − 5y = −10 in the xy-plane. What is the slope of line k?$q$, $q$["5/4","−5/4","−4/5","4/5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Solving for y gives y = −(4/5)x + 2, so the given line has slope −4/5. A perpendicular line has the negative reciprocal slope, 5/4.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-670$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in one variable$q$, 2, null, $q$In the equation 3(6x − k) = 18x − 24, k is a constant. If the equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of k?$q$, $q$["−24","8","−4/3","−8"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Distribute: 18x − 3k = 18x − 24. The x-terms already match, so the constants must match too: −3k = −24, giving k = 8.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-671$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$A food truck sold 87 meals in one day. The combo meals cost $12 each, and the single meals cost $7 each. If the total revenue was $724, how many single meals were sold?$q$, $q$["64","25","23","69"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Let a and s be the numbers of combo and single meals. Then a + s = 87 and 12a + 7s = 724. Substituting s = 87 − a gives 5a + 609 = 724, so a = 23 and s = 64.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-672$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in one variable$q$, 1, null, $q$If 3x + 2 = 29, what is the value of 6x + 4?$q$, $q$["29","56","9","58"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The expression 6x + 4 equals 2(3x + 2). Since 3x + 2 = 29, the value is 2(29) = 58.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-673$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$Line ℓ in the xy-plane has slope −2 and passes through the point (2, −2). Which of the following points also lies on line ℓ?$q$, $q$["(0, −6)","(0, 2)","(2, 0)","(0, −1)"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Moving from x = 2 to x = 0 changes x by −2, so y changes by −2 × −2 = 4. The new y-value is −2 + 4 = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-674$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$For the linear function f, f(3) = −10 and f(−1) = 14. What is the value of f(−6)?$q$, $q$["36","38","−44","44"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope is (14 − (−10))/(−1 − 3) = −6. Then f(x) = −6x + 8, so f(−6) = 44.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-675$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$Line k is parallel to the line with equation −x − 4y = −11 in the xy-plane. What is the slope of line k?$q$, $q$["−1/4","−4","1/4","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Solving for y gives y = −(1/4)x + 11/4, so the given line has slope −1/4. Parallel lines have equal slopes, so line k has slope −1/4.$q$, null),
