  ($q$alg-678$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation C = 120 + 2h gives the total cost, in dollars, of renting a kayak for h hours. What is the best interpretation of 2 in this context?$q$, $q$["The cost per hour to rent the kayak","The number of hours the kayak is rented","The total cost for 2 hours","The one-time fee for renting the kayak"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In the equation, 2 is multiplied by the variable, so it is the rate of change: the cost per hour to rent the kayak.$q$, null),
