  ($q$alg-680$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$<table class="data-table"><tr><th>x</th><th>f(x)</th></tr><tr><td>−1</td><td>−6</td></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>−7</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>−11</td></tr></table>The table shows three values of x and their corresponding values of f(x), where f is a linear function. Which equation defines f?$q$, $q$["f(x) = −x + 7","f(x) = −7x − 1","f(x) = x − 7","f(x) = −x − 7"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope is (−7 − (−6))/(0 − (−1)) = −1. Using x = −1: −6 = −1(−1) + b gives b = −7. So f(x) = −x − 7.$q$, null),
