  ($q$adv-284$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 9<sup>x</sup> = 3<sup>x − 1</sup>, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["1","−1","0","−3"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Both sides can be written with base 3: 9 = 3<sup>2</sup> and 3 = 3<sup>1</sup>. The equation becomes 3<sup>2x</sup> = 3<sup>1(x − 1)</sup>, so 2x = 1(x − 1). Solving this linear equation gives x = −1.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-285$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 7<sup>x</sup> = 343, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["3","6","49","2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$343 = 7³, so x = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-286$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 3<sup>x+2</sup> = 243, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["3","5","1","7"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$243 = 3⁵, so x + 2 = 5 → x = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-287$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 9<sup>x</sup> = 3<sup>x+4</sup>, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["4","8","2","−4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Write both sides with base 3: 9<sup>x</sup> = 3<sup>2x</sup>. Setting exponents equal: 2x = x + 4 → x = 4.$q$, null),
