  ($q$adv-306$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The polynomial f(x) = x³ − 3x² + x + k has x = 1 as one of its roots. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["1","−1","2","−2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$f(1) = 1 − 3 + 1 + k = −1 + k = 0 → k = 1.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-307$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function p is defined by p(x) = x³ − 2x² − 4x + d, where d is a constant. If p(4) = 18, what is the value of d?$q$, $q$["0","−2","2","3"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Substitute x = 4: p(4) = 4³ − 2(4)² − 4(4) + d = 18. Evaluating the numeric part and solving for d gives d = 2.$q$, null),
