  ($q$adv-309$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$When the polynomial p(x) = x³ + 4x² + 5x + 2 is divided by (x − −2), what is the remainder?$q$, $q$["−3","0","−1","1"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$By the Remainder Theorem, the remainder when p(x) is divided by (x − −2) equals p(−2). Computing p(−2) = −2³ + 4(−2)² + 5(−2) + 2 = 0.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-310$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The polynomial f(x) = x³ − 2x² − x + 2 can be factored as (x − 2)(x − 1)(x + 1). What is the sum of all its roots?$q$, $q$["2","0","−2","3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The roots are 2, 1, and −1, and their sum is 2 + 1 + (−1) = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-311$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = x³ + 2x² − 3x, for how many values of x does f(x) = 0?$q$, $q$["3","2","1","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Factoring: f(x) = x(x² + 2x − 3) = x(x + 3)(x − 1), so f(x) = 0 when x = 0, −3, or 1 — three values.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-312$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 1, null, $q$Which value of x satisfies the inequality x² − 1 < 0?$q$, $q$["0","2","−2","1.5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 1 = (x − 1)(x + 1) < 0 when −1 < x < 1. Only 0 falls in that interval.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-313$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what values of x is x² − 7x + 10 < 0?$q$, $q$["2 < x < 5","x < 2 or x > 5","−5 < x < −2","x < −5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Factoring: (x − 2)(x − 5) < 0. Since the parabola opens upward, the expression is negative between its roots, so 2 < x < 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-314$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what values of x is x² + 4x − 21 > 0?$q$, $q$["x < −7 or x > 3","−7 < x < 3","x < −3 or x > 7","x > 3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Factoring: (x + 7)(x − 3) > 0. Since the parabola opens upward, the expression is positive outside its roots, so x < −7 or x > 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-315$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 1, null, $q$Which value of x satisfies the inequality 2x² − 8 < 0?$q$, $q$["0","3","−3","2.5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$2x² − 8 < 0 → x² < 4 → −2 < x < 2. Only 0 falls in that interval.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-316$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what values of x is the inequality x² − 2x − 24 ≤ 0 true?$q$, $q$["−4 ≤ x ≤ 6","x ≤ −4 or x ≥ 6","−6 ≤ x ≤ 4","x ≤ −6 or x ≥ 4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Factoring: x² − 2x − 24 = (x − 6)(x + 4). Since the parabola opens upward, the expression is nonpositive between its roots, so −4 ≤ x ≤ 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-317$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what greatest integer value of k is x² + kx + 81 > 0 true for all real values of x?$q$, $q$["18","17","16","−17"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The quadratic x² + kx + 81 is positive for all real x exactly when its discriminant is negative: k² − 4(81) < 0, so k² < 324, meaning −18 < k < 18. The greatest integer satisfying this is 17.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-318$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$How many integer values of x satisfy x² + 6x + 5 < 0?$q$, $q$["4","5","3","2"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The inequality factors as (x − −5)(x − −1) < 0, which holds for −5 < x < −1. The integers strictly between −5 and −1 number 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-319$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$Which value of x satisfies the inequality x² − 6x + 8 > 0?$q$, $q$["5","3","2.5","3.5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 6x + 8 = (x − 2)(x − 4) > 0 when x < 2 or x > 4. Only 5 falls outside the interval [2, 4].$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-320$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = x + 2 and g(x) = 5x, what is the value of f(g(1))?$q$, $q$["7","15","10","6"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(1) = 5(1) = 5, so f(g(1)) = f(5) = 5 + 2 = 7.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-321$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = 4x and g(x) = x − 3, what is the value of g(f(2))?$q$, $q$["5","8","2","20"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$f(2) = 4(2) = 8, so g(f(2)) = g(8) = 8 − 3 = 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-322$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = x² + 1 and g(x) = 2x − 1, what is the value of f(g(2))?$q$, $q$["10","9","7","5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(2) = 2(2) − 1 = 3, so f(g(2)) = f(3) = 3² + 1 = 10.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-323$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = −5x + 1 and g(x) = 5x + 5, what is the value of f(g(6))?$q$, $q$["174","−172","−140","−174"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$First, g(6) = 5(6) + 5 = 35. Then f(35) = −5(35) + 1 = −174.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-324$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = x² − 4 and g(x) = x + 1, what is the value of f(g(−3))?$q$, $q$["0","−3","5","−8"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(−3) = −3 + 1 = −2, so f(g(−3)) = f(−2) = (−2)² − 4 = 0.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-325$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = 3x + 2 and g(x) = x² − x, what is the value of g(f(0))?$q$, $q$["2","6","4","0"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$f(0) = 3(0) + 2 = 2, so g(f(0)) = g(2) = 2² − 2 = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-326$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = x + 3 and g(x) = −x − 4, and f(g(x)) = −6, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−5","5","3","6"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$f(g(x)) = 1(−x − 4) + 3 = −x − 1. Setting this equal to −6 gives x = 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-327$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If y = x² + 4 and y = 4x, what is the value of x that satisfies both equations?$q$, $q$["2","−2","4","−4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² + 4 = 4x → x² − 4x + 4 = 0 → (x − 2)² = 0, so x = 2 is the only solution.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-328$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² + 2x and y = 3x, what is the greatest value of x that satisfies both equations?$q$, $q$["1","0","−1","3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² + 2x = 3x → x² − x = 0 → x(x − 1) = 0, so x = 0 or x = 1. The greatest value is 1.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-329$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² − 1 and y = 3x + 3, what is the sum of all values of x that satisfy both equations?$q$, $q$["3","4","−1","5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 1 = 3x + 3 → x² − 3x − 4 = 0 → (x − 4)(x + 1) = 0, so x = 4 or x = −1. Their sum is 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-330$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² − 2x − 3 and y = 2x − 3, what is the sum of all values of x that satisfy both equations?$q$, $q$["4","0","−4","2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 2x − 3 = 2x − 3 → x² − 4x = 0 → x(x − 4) = 0, so x = 0 or x = 4. Their sum is 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-331$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the product of the x-coordinates of the solutions to the system y = x² − x + 3 and y = −2x + 8?$q$, $q$["−2","−5","1","5"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Setting the expressions for y equal gives x² + (−1 − −2)x + (3 − 8) = 0, i.e., x² + x − 5 = 0. By Vieta's formulas, the product of the roots is −5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-332$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² + 2x − 1 and y = 4x − 1, what is the sum of all values of x that satisfy both equations?$q$, $q$["2","0","−2","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² + 2x − 1 = 4x − 1 → x² − 2x = 0 → x(x − 2) = 0, so x = 0 or x = 2. Their sum is 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-333$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$How many real solutions does the system y = x² + 3x + 2 and y = 2x − 7 have?$q$, $q$["3","2","0","1"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Substituting gives x² + (3 − 2)x + (2 − −7) = 0, i.e., x² + x + 9 = 0, with discriminant 1² − 4(9) = −35. Since the discriminant is negative, the system has 0 real solutions.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-334$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 1, null, $q$A population is modeled by P(t) = 600(1.2)<sup>t</sup>, where t is measured in years. What is the population, to the nearest whole number, after 2 years?$q$, $q$["864","720","600","960"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$P(2) = 600(1.2)² = 600(1.44) = 864.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-335$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A car depreciates in value according to V(t) = 18000(0.9)<sup>t</sup>, where t is measured in years. To the nearest hundred dollars, what is the car's value after 2 years?$q$, $q$["$14,600","$16,200","$14,500","$15,000"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$V(2) = 18000(0.9)² = 18000(0.81) = 14,580, which rounds to $14,600.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-336$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The number of bacteria in a culture doubles every 7 hours. If there are 400 bacteria at time t = 0 (in hours), which function models the number of bacteria, B(t), after t hours?$q$, $q$["B(t) = 400 · 2<sup>t/7</sup>","B(t) = 400 · 2<sup>7t</sup>","B(t) = 400 · 7<sup>t/2</sup>","B(t) = 400 · 2<sup>t</sup>"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Doubling every 7 hours means the exponent is t/7: B(t) = 400 · 2<sup>t/7</sup>. Check: B(7) = 400 · 2¹ = 800, double the original amount.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-337$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f(x) = 60(0.4)<sup>x</sup> models exponential decay. What is the decay factor?$q$, $q$["0.4","60","0.6","1.4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In a function of the form f(x) = a(b)<sup>x</sup> representing decay, b is the decay factor. Here b = 0.4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-338$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A quantity is modeled by P(t) = 30 · r<sup>t</sup>. If P(2) = 270 and r is a positive constant with P(4) = 2430, what is the value of P(2)/P(0)?$q$, $q$["9","4.5","18","10"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Dividing, P(4)/P(2) = r<sup>2</sup> = 2430/270 = 9. Since P(0) = 30 and P(2) = 30 · r<sup>2</sup>, the ratio P(2)/P(0) is simply r<sup>2</sup> = 9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-339$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If x² − 13x + 30 = 0, what is the sum of the solutions?$q$, $q$["13","30","−13","10"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 13x + 30 = (x − 3)(x − 10), so the roots are 3 and 10, and their sum is 13.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-340$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 3x² − 4x − 4 = 0, what is the product of the solutions?$q$, $q$["−4/3","4/3","2","−2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$3x² − 4x − 4 = (3x + 2)(x − 2) = 0, so x = −2/3 or x = 2. Their product is −2/3 · 2 = −4/3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-341$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If x² + 6x + 9 = 0, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−3","3","−9","9"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² + 6x + 9 = (x + 3)² = 0, so x = −3 is the only solution.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-342$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$For the equation x² − x − 56 = 0, what is the sum of the squares of its two solutions?$q$, $q$["1","113","112","109"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$By Vieta's formulas, the sum of the solutions is 1 and the product is −56. The sum of the squares of the solutions equals (sum)² − 2(product) = 1² − 2(−56) = 113.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-343$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f(x) = (x − 4)² − 6 has what minimum value?$q$, $q$["−6","4","6","−4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In vertex form (x − h)² + k, the minimum value is k = −6, occurring at x = 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-344$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$For the function f(x) = −x² − 2x − 9, what is the average rate of change of f from x = 2 to x = 3?$q$, $q$["−3","−5","−7","7"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The average rate of change equals (f(3) − f(2))/(3 − 2). For a quadratic ax² + bx + c, this simplifies to a(2 + 3) + b = −1(5) − 2 = −7.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-345$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (6x⁵)(3x²)?$q$, $q$["18x<sup>7</sup>","9x<sup>7</sup>","18x<sup>10</sup>","9x<sup>10</sup>"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Multiply coefficients and add exponents: 6·3 = 18, and x⁵·x² = x<sup>7</sup>, giving 18x<sup>7</sup>.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-346$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (x + 6)(x − 6) + 36?$q$, $q$["x<sup>2</sup>","x<sup>2</sup> − 36","x<sup>2</sup> + 36","x<sup>2</sup> + 12x"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$(x + 6)(x − 6) = x² − 36, and adding 36 gives x² − 36 + 36 = x².$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-347$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If x² − 10x + 21 = 0, what is the product of the solutions?$q$, $q$["21","10","−21","−10"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 10x + 21 = (x − 3)(x − 7), so the roots are 3 and 7, and their product is 21.$q$, null),
