  ($q$adv-352$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² − 1 and y = 3x − 3, what is the sum of all values of x that satisfy both equations?$q$, $q$["3","2","1","−3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 1 = 3x − 3 → x² − 3x + 2 = 0 → (x − 1)(x − 2) = 0, so x = 1 or x = 2. Their sum is 3.$q$, null),
