  ($q$adv-362$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = 2x³ + 3x² − 5, what is the value of f(−2)?$q$, $q$["−9","−21","3","11"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$f(−2) = 2(−8) + 3(4) − 5 = −16 + 12 − 5 = −9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-363$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = x² − 1 and g(x) = x + 3, what is the value of f(g(−1))?$q$, $q$["3","2","−1","8"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(−1) = −1 + 3 = 2, and f(2) = 2² − 1 = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-364$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (x + 5)(x − 5) + 25?$q$, $q$["x<sup>2</sup>","x<sup>2</sup> − 25","x<sup>2</sup> + 25","x<sup>2</sup> + 10x"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$(x + 5)(x − 5) = x² − 25, and adding 25 gives x² − 25 + 25 = x².$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-365$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If (x − 7)² = 49, what is the positive value of x?$q$, $q$["14","0","7","49"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$(x − 7)² = 49 means x − 7 = ±7, so x = 14 or x = 0. The positive value is 14.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-366$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what values of x is the inequality 2x² + 7x − 4 ≥ 0 true?$q$, $q$["x ≤ −4 or x ≥ 1/2","−4 ≤ x ≤ 1/2","x ≤ −1/2 or x ≥ 4","−1/2 ≤ x ≤ 4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$2x² + 7x − 4 = (2x − 1)(x + 4) = 0 at x = 1/2 and x = −4. Since the parabola opens upward, the expression is ≥ 0 outside the roots: x ≤ −4 or x ≥ 1/2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-367$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 9<sup>x+1</sup> = 3<sup>x+5</sup>, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["3","1","5","−1"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Write 9 as 3²: 3<sup>2(x+1)</sup> = 3<sup>x+5</sup>, so 2x + 2 = x + 5, giving x = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-368$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A population is modeled by P(t) = 400 · r<sup>t</sup>, where t is measured in years and r is a positive constant. If P(3) = 50, what is the value of r?$q$, $q$["0.125","0.5","1","−0.5"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$P(3) = 400 · r<sup>3</sup> = 50, so r<sup>3</sup> = 0.125, which gives r = 0.5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-369$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The graph of y = −4(x − 2)² + 9 is a parabola. What is the maximum value of y?$q$, $q$["9","2","−9","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Since the coefficient −4 is negative, the parabola opens downward and reaches a maximum of 9 at x = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-370$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the sum of the x-coordinates of the solutions to the system y = x² + 5x + 5 and y = −4x + 9?$q$, $q$["−10","−9","9","−7"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Setting the expressions for y equal gives x² + 5x + 5 = −4x + 9, or x² + (5 − −4)x + (5 − 9) = 0, i.e., x² + 9x − 4 = 0. By Vieta's formulas, the sum of the roots is −9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-371$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The polynomial p(x) = x³ + 3x² + mx − 6 has (x − −3) as a factor, where m is a constant. What is the value of m?$q$, $q$["2","−2","−1","−4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$By the Factor Theorem, (x − −3) is a factor of p(x) exactly when p(−3) = 0: −3³ + 3(−3)² + m(−3) − 6 = 0. Solving gives m = −2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-372$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$If f(x) = −3x + 8 and g(x) = −3x + 6, and g(f(x)) = px + q for constants p and q, what is the value of p + q?$q$, $q$["9","−9","−7","27"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$g(f(x)) = −3(−3x + 8) + 6 = 9x − 18. So p = 9 and q = −18, giving p + q = −9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-373$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to 9x² − 16?$q$, $q$["(3x − 4)²","(3x − 4)(3x + 4)","(3x − 16)(3x + 1)","(9x − 4)(x + 4)"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$9x² − 16 = (3x)² − 4² is a difference of squares, which factors as (3x − 4)(3x + 4).$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-374$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$For what negative value of k does the equation x² + kx + 64 = 0 have exactly one real solution?$q$, $q$["−16","16","−8","8"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$One real solution requires the discriminant to equal 0: k² − 4(1)(64) = 0 → k² = 256 → k = ±16. The negative value is −16.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-375$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 1, null, $q$Which value of x satisfies the inequality x² − 9x + 20 < 0?$q$, $q$["4.5","3","6","10"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 9x + 20 = (x − 4)(x − 5), which is negative when 4 < x < 5. Only x = 4.5 lies in that interval.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-376$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 6<sup>x</sup> = 216, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["3","6","36","2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$216 = 6³, so x = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-377$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A car valued at $24,000 depreciates at a rate of 15% per year. To the nearest dollar, what is the car's value after 2 years?$q$, $q$["$17,340","$20,400","$16,800","$18,000"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Each year the value is multiplied by 1 − 0.15 = 0.85. After 2 years: 24,000(0.85)² = 24,000(0.7225) = 17,340.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-378$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$For what value of x does the function f(x) = 2x² − 12x + 7 reach its minimum value?$q$, $q$["3","6","−3","12"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The minimum occurs at x = −b/(2a) = 12/(2·2) = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-379$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² + 1 and y = 5x − 5, what is the sum of all values of x that satisfy both equations?$q$, $q$["5","2","3","6"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² + 1 = 5x − 5 → x² − 5x + 6 = 0 → (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0, so x = 2 or x = 3. Their sum is 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-380$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = x⁴ − 3x² + 2, what is the value of f(−1)?$q$, $q$["0","6","−4","4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$f(−1) = (−1)<sup>4</sup> − 3(−1)² + 2 = 1 − 3 + 2 = 0.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-381$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = x² and g(x) = f(x + 2) − 5, what is the value of g(1)?$q$, $q$["4","9","−5","14"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(1) = f(1 + 2) − 5 = f(3) − 5 = 9 − 5 = 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-382$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (2x⁴)(5x²)?$q$, $q$["10x<sup>6</sup>","7x<sup>6</sup>","10x<sup>8</sup>","7x<sup>8</sup>"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Multiply coefficients and add exponents: 2·5 = 10, and x⁴·x² = x<sup>6</sup>, giving 10x<sup>6</sup>.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-383$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the product of the solutions to 6x² + 11x + 3 = 0?$q$, $q$["−11/7","−1/2","11/7","1/2"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$For 6x² + 11x + 3 = 0, Vieta's formulas give the sum of the solutions as −b/a = −11/6 and the product as c/a = 1/2. So the product is 1/2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-384$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what greatest integer value of k is x² + kx + 100 > 0 true for all real values of x?$q$, $q$["18","20","19","−19"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The quadratic x² + kx + 100 is positive for all real x exactly when its discriminant is negative: k² − 4(100) < 0, so k² < 400, meaning −20 < k < 20. The greatest integer satisfying this is 19.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-385$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 25<sup>x + 6</sup> = 5<sup>x + 8</sup>, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−3","4","−4","−6"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Both sides can be written with base 5: 25 = 5<sup>2</sup> and 5 = 5<sup>1</sup>. The equation becomes 5<sup>2(x + 6)</sup> = 5<sup>1(x + 8)</sup>, so 2(x + 6) = 1(x + 8). Solving this linear equation gives x = −4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-386$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function g(x) = 4(3)<sup>x</sup> is evaluated at x = 0. What is the value of g(0)?$q$, $q$["4","0","3","1"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Any nonzero base raised to the 0 power equals 1, so g(0) = 4(3)<sup>0</sup> = 4(1) = 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-387$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function g is defined by g(x) = f(x − −2) − 3, where f(x) = −5x² + 6x + 6. What is the value of g(−5)?$q$, $q$["−57","−61","−60","60"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$g(−5) = f(−5 − −2) − 3 = f(−3) − 3. Since f(−3) = −5(−3)² + 6(−3) + 6 = −57, g(−5) = −57 − 3 = −60.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-388$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If y = x² and y = 49, what is the positive value of x that satisfies both equations?$q$, $q$["7","49","−7","14"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² = 49 means x = 7 or x = −7; the positive value is 7.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-389$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = x³ + 5, what is the value of f(−1)?$q$, $q$["4","6","−4","−6"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$f(−1) = (−1)³ + 5 = −1 + 5 = 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-390$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = 3x − 4 and g(x) = x + 2, what is the value of f(g(0))?$q$, $q$["2","−4","6","0"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(0) = 0 + 2 = 2, and f(2) = 3(2) − 4 = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-391$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to √(18x⁴), for x ≥ 0?$q$, $q$["3x²√2","9x²√2","3x√2","6x²"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$√(18x⁴) = √9 · √2 · √(x⁴) = 3x²√2, since x⁴ = (x²)² is a perfect square.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-392$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 4x² − 9 = 0, what is the positive value of x?$q$, $q$["3/2","9/4","9/2","4/9"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$4x² − 9 = (2x − 3)(2x + 3) = 0, so x = 3/2 or x = −3/2. The positive value is 3/2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-393$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$For what values of x is the inequality x² + x − 12 > 0 true?$q$, $q$["x < −4 or x > 3","−4 < x < 3","x < −3 or x > 4","−3 < x < 4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² + x − 12 = (x + 4)(x − 3), which is positive outside the roots, so x < −4 or x > 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-394$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 5<sup>x</sup> · 5<sup>3</sup> = 5<sup>9</sup>, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["6","3","9","12"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$5<sup>x</sup> · 5<sup>3</sup> = 5<sup>x+3</sup> = 5<sup>9</sup>, so x + 3 = 9, giving x = 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-395$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The number of subscribers to a streaming channel doubles every 3 months. If the channel starts with 150 subscribers, which function models the number of subscribers, S(m), after m months?$q$, $q$["S(m) = 150(2)<sup>m/3</sup>","S(m) = 150(2)<sup>3m</sup>","S(m) = 150(3)<sup>m/2</sup>","S(m) = 150(2)<sup>m</sup>"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Doubling every 3 months means the growth factor per month is 2<sup>1/3</sup>, so after m months the count is multiplied by 2<sup>m/3</sup>: S(m) = 150(2)<sup>m/3</sup>.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-396$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f(x) = (x − 1)² + 8 has what minimum value?$q$, $q$["8","1","−8","−1"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In vertex form (x − h)² + k, the minimum value is k = 8, occurring at x = 1.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-397$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If y = x² − 4x and y = 2x − 8, what is the sum of all values of x that satisfy both equations?$q$, $q$["6","2","4","8"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$x² − 4x = 2x − 8 → x² − 6x + 8 = 0 → (x − 2)(x − 4) = 0, so x = 2 or x = 4. Their sum is 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-398$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The polynomial g(x) = x³ − 6x² + 11x − 6 has roots at x = 1, 2, and 3. What is the value of g(0)?$q$, $q$["−6","6","0","−11"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Since g(x) = (x − 1)(x − 2)(x − 3), g(0) = (−1)(−2)(−3) = −6, which matches the constant term of g.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-399$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 1, null, $q$If f(x) = x² + x and g(x) = 2x − 1, what is the value of f(g(1))?$q$, $q$["2","1","6","3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$g(1) = 2(1) − 1 = 1, and f(1) = 1² + 1 = 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-400$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$The expression x² − 12x + 8 is equivalent to (x + h)² + k, where h and k are constants. What is the value of h + k?$q$, $q$["−32","−34","22","34"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Completing the square: x² − 12x + 8 = (x − 6)² + (8 − 36) = (x − 6)² − 28. So h = −6 and k = −28, giving h + k = −34.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-401$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation 3x² − 12x + k = 0 has exactly one real solution. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["12","9","−12","15"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A quadratic has exactly one real solution when its discriminant is 0: −12² − 4(3)(k) = 0, so k = −12²/(4·3) = 12. (This matches 3(x − 2)², whose only root is x = 2.)$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-402$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A quantity is modeled by P(t) = 900 · r<sup>t</sup>. If P(2) = 8100 and r is a positive constant with P(3) = 24300, what is the value of P(1)/P(0)?$q$, $q$["1.5","6","3","4"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Dividing, P(3)/P(2) = r<sup>1</sup> = 24300/8100 = 3. Since P(0) = 900 and P(1) = 900 · r<sup>1</sup>, the ratio P(1)/P(0) is simply r<sup>1</sup> = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-403$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function y = −x² + 10x − 21 has what maximum value?$q$, $q$["4","25","−21","5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$y = −(x² − 10x) − 21 = −(x − 5)² + 25 − 21 = −(x − 5)² + 4, so the maximum value is 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-404$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (3x²y)(4xy³)?$q$, $q$["12x³y⁴","7x³y⁴","12x²y³","7x²y³"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Multiply coefficients and add exponents of matching variables: 3·4 = 12, x²·x¹ = x³, y¹·y³ = y⁴, giving 12x³y⁴.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-405$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 2x² = 50, what is the positive value of x?$q$, $q$["5","25","10","50"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$2x² = 50 → x² = 25 → x = 5 or x = −5. The positive value is 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-406$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$For the function f(x) = x² − 2x + 1, what is the average rate of change of f from x = −6 to x = 0?$q$, $q$["8","−6","4","−8"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The average rate of change equals (f(0) − f(−6))/(0 − −6). For a quadratic ax² + bx + c, this simplifies to a(−6) + b = 1(−6) − 2 = −8.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-407$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (4x⁶)/(2x²), for x ≠ 0?$q$, $q$["2x<sup>4</sup>","2x<sup>3</sup>","6x<sup>4</sup>","6x<sup>3</sup>"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Divide coefficients and subtract exponents: 4/2 = 2, and x⁶/x² = x⁴, giving 2x⁴.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-408$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f(x) = 3(x + 4)² − 1 has what minimum value?$q$, $q$["−1","4","−4","1"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The minimum value is k = −1, occurring at x = −4; the coefficient 3 only affects steepness, not the minimum value.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-409$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (x − 4)² − (x + 4)²?$q$, $q$["−16x","0","32","−8x"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$(x − 4)² = x² − 8x + 16 and (x + 4)² = x² + 8x + 16. Subtracting: (x² − 8x + 16) − (x² + 8x + 16) = −16x.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-410$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (5x + 3)² − (5x − 3)²?$q$, $q$["50x² + 18","18","60x + 18","60x"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Use a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b) with a = 5x + 3 and b = 5x − 3: (2·3)(2·5x) = 60x. (Or expand: the squares' x² and constant terms cancel, leaving 60x.)$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-411$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The polynomial p(x) = x³ − 2x² − 5x + k, where k is a constant, has x − 2 as a factor. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["12","−10","11","10"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$If x − 2 is a factor, then p(2) = 0: 8 − 8 − 10 + k = 0, so k = 10.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-412$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function p is defined by p(x) = (x − 1)(x + 2)(x − 3). What is the sum of the zeros of p?$q$, $q$["−2","6","2","−4"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The zeros are x = 1, x = −2, and x = 3, so their sum is 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-413$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A ball is thrown upward. Its height h, in feet, t seconds after being thrown is given by h(t) = −16t² + 80t + 6. What is the maximum height, in feet, of the ball?$q$, $q$["106","5/2","112","86"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The maximum occurs at t = 80/32 = 5/2. Then h = −16(5/2)² + 80(5/2) + 6 = 106.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-414$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$y = x² − x + 4
y = −x + 8

In the xy-plane, the graphs of the given equations intersect at two points. What is the sum of the x-coordinates of the two points of intersection?$q$, $q$["0","−1","1","−4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Setting the expressions equal: x² − 4 = 0. The sum of the roots is the opposite of the x-coefficient: 0.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-415$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 1, null, $q$For x ≠ 0, which expression is equivalent to (x^5)^3 / x^2?$q$, $q$["x^6","x^13","x^10","x^17"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$(x^5)^3 = x^15. Dividing by x^2 subtracts exponents: x^13.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-416$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A radioactive sample has a half-life of 6 days. If the sample's mass is 160 grams initially, what is its mass, in grams, after 18 days?$q$, $q$["40","140","80","20"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$18 days is 3 half-lives, so the mass is 160·(1/2)^3 = 20 grams.$q$, null),
