  ($q$adv-425$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation 3x² + kx + 3 = 0 has exactly one real solution, where k is a positive constant. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["6","7","12","36"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The discriminant must be 0: k² − 4(3)(3) = 0, so k² = 36 and k = 6 (k is positive).$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-426$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (4x + 4)² − (4x − 4)²?$q$, $q$["32","64x","32x² + 32","64x + 32"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Use a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b) with a = 4x + 4 and b = 4x − 4: (2·4)(2·4x) = 64x. (Or expand: the squares' x² and constant terms cancel, leaving 64x.)$q$, null),
