  ($q$adv-432$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$In the equation x² + 18x + c = 0, c is a constant. If the equation has exactly one real solution, what is the value of c?$q$, $q$["9","81","18","36"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$One real solution means the discriminant is zero: 18² − 4c = 0, so c = 324/4 = 81.$q$, null),
