  ($q$adv-656$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$The expression (x + 3)² − (x + 2)² can be written as px + q, where p and q are constants. What is the value of p + q?$q$, $q$["5","2","10","7"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$(x² + 6x + 9) − (x² + 4x + 4) = 2x + 5. So p + q = 7.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-657$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 2, null, $q$If 3ˣ = n, where n is a positive number, which expression is equal to 3^(x + 3)?$q$, $q$["n + 3","n^3","27n","3n"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$3^(x + 3) = 3ˣ · 3^3 = n · 27 = 27n.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-658$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 2, null, $q$When p(x) = 3x³ − 2x² − x + 8 is divided by x − 2, what is the remainder?$q$, $q$["22","8","24","−22"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$By the remainder theorem, the remainder is p(2) = 3(8) − 8 − 2 + 8 = 22.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-659$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f is defined by f(x) = -2(x − 4)² + 7. The graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane has its vertex at (h, k). What is the value of h + k?$q$, $q$["11","−11","3","−3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In vertex form a(x − h)² + k, the vertex is (h, k). Here the vertex is (4, 7), so h + k = 11.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-660$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the sum of the solutions to x² − 5x − 14 = 0?$q$, $q$["6","−5","5","−14"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Factor: x² − 5x − 14 = (x + 2)(x − 7), so the solutions are −2 and 7. Their sum is 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-661$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f(t) = 8000(1.02)^t gives the number of members of a club t months after the start of a study. Which statement best describes how f changes?$q$, $q$["It increases by 2 each month.","It increases by 1.02% each month.","It decreases by 2% each month.","It increases by 2% each month."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$In f(t) = a(b)^t, the base b = 1.02 is 1 + 0.02, so f is multiplied by 1.02 each month. That is a 2% increase per month.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-662$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f(t) = 1200(1.15)^t gives the number of members of a club t years after the start of a study. Which statement best describes how f changes?$q$, $q$["It increases by 1.15% each year.","It increases by 15 each year.","It decreases by 15% each year.","It increases by 15% each year."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$In f(t) = a(b)^t, the base b = 1.15 is 1 + 0.15, so f is multiplied by 1.15 each year. That is a 15% increase per year.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-663$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$How many integer values of x satisfy (x + 1)(x − 5) ≤ 0?$q$, $q$["5","8","7","6"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The product is zero or negative when x is between the roots −1 and 5, inclusive. The integers −1 through 5 number 7.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-664$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f is defined by f(x) = 2x² + 20x + 41. What is the minimum value of f?$q$, $q$["−9","41","59","−5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The vertex occurs at x = −b/(2a) = −20/4 = −5. Then f(−5) = −9. Because the parabola opens upward, the minimum value is −9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-665$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 5^(x + 4) = 3125, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["9","1","621","5"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Since 3125 = 5^5, the exponents must be equal: x + 4 = 5, so x = 1.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-666$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the value of 125^(1/3)?$q$, $q$["5","125/3","1/5","−5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$125^(1/3) = (the cube root of 125)^1 = 5^1 = 5.$q$, null),
