  ($q$adv-668$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the sum of the solutions to 3x² + 6x − 45 = 0?$q$, $q$["6","−15","−2","2"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Factor: 3x² + 6x − 45 = 3(x + 5)(x − 3), so the solutions are −5 and 3. Their sum is −2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-669$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Polynomial functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function p is defined by p(x) = −2x³ − 3x² + x + 2. What is the value of p(3)?$q$, $q$["2","26","−76","−80"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Substitute 3 for x and evaluate each term: p(3) = −54 − 27 + 3 + 2 = −76.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-670$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (3x⁵)(7x⁴)?$q$, $q$["10x⁹","21x²⁰","21x⁹","21x"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Multiply the coefficients (3 × 7 = 21) and add the exponents of x (5 + 4 = 9).$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-671$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to 3x² − 243?$q$, $q$["3(x − 9)(x − 9)","3(x + 9)(x − 9)","3(x − 9)(x + 9)","(3x − 9)(x + 9)"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Factor out 3: 3(x² − 81). Two numbers with product −81 and sum 0 are −9 and 9, giving 3(x − 9)(x + 9).$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-672$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f is defined by f(x) = −2x² − 3x + 4. What is the value of f(−4)?$q$, $q$["32","48","8","−16"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Substitute −4 for x: f(−4) = −2(−4)² − 3(−4) + 4 = −32 + 12 + 4 = −16.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-673$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$For the exponential function f, f(0) = 4 and f(2) = 64. What is the value of f(2)?$q$, $q$["16","256","32","64"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$f(x) = a·b^x with a = f(0) = 4. Since f(2) = 4·b² = 64, b² = 16 and b = 4. So f(2) = 4·4^2 = 64.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-674$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 25^(x + 6) = 5^(3x), what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["12","3","12/5","−12"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Write 25 as 5^2: 5^(2(x + 6)) = 5^(3x). Equate exponents: 2x + 12 = 3x, so x = 12.$q$, null),
