  ($q$adv-676$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the product of the solutions to 3x² − 3x − 90 = 0?$q$, $q$["1","−90","30","−30"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Factor: 3x² − 3x − 90 = 3(x − 6)(x + 5), so the solutions are 6 and −5. Their product is −30.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-677$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$How many distinct real solutions does the equation −2x² − 4x + 3 = 0 have?$q$, $q$["Exactly two distinct real solutions","No real solutions","Infinitely many solutions","Exactly one real solution"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The discriminant is b² − 4ac = (−4)² − 4(−2)(3) = 40. A positive discriminant means two distinct real solutions.$q$, null),
