  ($q$adv-679$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 4^(x + 1) = 2^(4x), what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["2","−1","1","1/3"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Write 4 as 2^2: 2^(2(x + 1)) = 2^(4x). Equate exponents: 2x + 2 = 4x, so 2x = 2 and x = 1.$q$, null),
