  ($q$adv-686$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f(t) = 3000(0.95)^t models the population of a town t years after it was first measured. What is the best interpretation of 3000 in this context?$q$, $q$["The amount after 0.95 years","The amount after one year","The amount when it was first measured","The change in the amount each year"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$When t = 0, f(0) = 3000(0.95)^0 = 3000. So 3000 is the amount at the time of the first measurement.$q$, null),
