  ($q$adv-690$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$y = x² − 3x − 28<br>y = −x − 4<br><br>The graphs of the equations above intersect at two points. What is the sum of the x-coordinates of the intersection points?$q$, $q$["2","−2","−24","3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Set the expressions equal: x² − 3x − 28 = −x − 4, so x² − 2x − 24 = 0. This factors as (x + 4)(x − 6) = 0, so x = −4 or x = 6. The sum is 2.$q$, null),
