  ($q$adv-709$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$How many integer values of x satisfy (x + 3)x < 0?$q$, $q$["4","1","3","2"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The product is negative when x is strictly between the roots −3 and 0. The integers −2 through −1 number 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-710$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$y = x² + 12x + 18<br>y = 4x + 6<br><br>The graphs of the equations above intersect at two points. What is the sum of the x-coordinates of the intersection points?$q$, $q$["−8","−12","8","12"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Set the expressions equal: x² + 12x + 18 = 4x + 6, so x² + 8x + 12 = 0. This factors as (x + 2)(x + 6) = 0, so x = −2 or x = −6. The sum is −8.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-711$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 27^(x − 5) = 3^(2x), what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−15","−3","15","−5"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Write 27 as 3^3: 3^(3(x − 5)) = 3^(2x). Equate exponents: 3x − 15 = 2x, so −x = −15 and x = 15.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-712$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$How many integer values of x satisfy x(x − 4) < 0?$q$, $q$["2","3","4","5"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The product is negative when x is strictly between the roots 0 and 4. The integers 1 through 3 number 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-713$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f is defined by f(x) = −3x² + 4x − 5. What is the value of f(2)?$q$, $q$["9","−25","7","−9"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Substitute 2 for x: f(2) = −3(2)² + 4(2) − 5 = −12 + 8 − 5 = −9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-714$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$How many distinct real solutions does the equation −2x² + 3x + 9 = 0 have?$q$, $q$["Exactly two distinct real solutions","Exactly one real solution","No real solutions","Infinitely many solutions"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The discriminant is b² − 4ac = (3)² − 4(−2)(9) = 81. A positive discriminant means two distinct real solutions.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-715$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (−5x² − 4x + 3) − (4x² − 5x − 3)?$q$, $q$["−9x² − 9x","−x² − 9x","−9x² + x + 6","−9x² + x"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Distribute the subtraction to every term of the second polynomial, then combine like terms: x² terms give −9x², x terms give x, and constants give 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-716$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential equations$q$, 2, null, $q$If 8^(x − 6) = 2^(5x), what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−3/2","−9/4","9","−9"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Write 8 as 2^3: 2^(3(x − 6)) = 2^(5x). Equate exponents: 3x − 18 = 5x, so 2x = −18 and x = −9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-717$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f(t) = 8000(1.05)^t gives the number of fish in a lake t years after the start of a study. Which statement best describes how f changes?$q$, $q$["It increases by 5% each year.","It increases by 5 each year.","It increases by 1.05% each year.","It decreases by 5% each year."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In f(t) = a(b)^t, the base b = 1.05 is 1 + 0.05, so f is multiplied by 1.05 each year. That is a 5% increase per year.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-718$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the solution to the equation √(3x + 1) = 4?$q$, $q$["5","1","17/3","16/3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Square both sides: 3x + 1 = 16. Subtract 1 from both sides to get 3x = 15, so x = 5. Checking, √(16) = 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-719$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f(t) = 650(1.06)^t gives the value, in dollars, of an investment t months after the start of a study. Which statement best describes how f changes?$q$, $q$["It increases by 6% each month.","It increases by 6 each month.","It increases by 1.06% each month.","It decreases by 6% each month."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In f(t) = a(b)^t, the base b = 1.06 is 1 + 0.06, so f is multiplied by 1.06 each month. That is a 6% increase per month.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-720$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the value of 64^(−1/3)?$q$, $q$["4","−64/3","1/4","−1/4"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$64^(−1/3) = (the cube root of 64)^(−1) = 4^(−1) = 1/4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-721$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (8x² − 3x + 7) + (−x² + 5x − 3)?$q$, $q$["7x² + 2x + 6","7x² + 2x + 4","9x² − 8x + 10","7x² + 2x + 10"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Combine like terms: x² terms give 7x², x terms give 2x, and constants give 4.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-722$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$What is the positive solution to the equation 3x² + 8 = 440?$q$, $q$["440/3","12","20","144"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Subtract 8 from both sides: 3x² = 432, so x² = 144. Taking the positive square root gives x = 12.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-723$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to x² − 64?$q$, $q$["(x − 8)(x − 8)","(x + 8)(x + 8)","(x + 8)(x − 8)","(x − 8)(x + 8)"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Look for two numbers with product −64 and sum 0: they are −8 and 8. So the expression is (x − 8)(x + 8).$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-724$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f is defined by f(x) = −(x + 3)² + 6. The graph of y = f(x) in the xy-plane has its vertex at (h, k). What is the value of h + k?$q$, $q$["3","−9","−3","9"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$In vertex form a(x − h)² + k, the vertex is (h, k). Here the vertex is (−3, 6), so h + k = 3.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-725$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the value of 36^(−1/2)?$q$, $q$["−1/6","6","1/6","−18"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$36^(−1/2) = (the square root of 36)^(−1) = 6^(−1) = 1/6.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-726$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Function composition$q$, 2, null, $q$The functions f and g are defined by f(x) = 2x − 3 and g(x) = 2x² − 5. What is the value of f(g(3))?$q$, $q$["23","25","13","39"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$First, g(3) = 13. Then f(13) = 2(13) − 3 = 23.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-727$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 2, null, $q$How many distinct real solutions does the equation −x² + 6x − 6 = 0 have?$q$, $q$["Infinitely many solutions","Exactly two distinct real solutions","No real solutions","Exactly one real solution"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The discriminant is b² − 4ac = (6)² − 4(−1)(−6) = 12. A positive discriminant means two distinct real solutions.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-728$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f is defined by f(x) = −2x² + 3x − 6. What is the value of f(−1)?$q$, $q$["−11","−17","−7","−5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Substitute −1 for x: f(−1) = −2(−1)² + 3(−1) − 6 = −2 − 3 − 6 = −11.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-729$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$What is the positive solution to the equation 2x² + 3 = 131?$q$, $q$["131/2","64","8","11"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Subtract 3 from both sides: 2x² = 128, so x² = 64. Taking the positive square root gives x = 8.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-730$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f(t) = 2400(0.9)^t models the population of a town t years after it was first measured. What is the best interpretation of 2400 in this context?$q$, $q$["The amount after one year","The change in the amount each year","The amount after 0.9 years","The amount when it was first measured"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$When t = 0, f(0) = 2400(0.9)^0 = 2400. So 2400 is the amount at the time of the first measurement.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-731$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (4x³)³?$q$, $q$["12x⁹","64x⁹","4x⁹","64x⁶"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Raise each factor to the power 3: 4^3 = 64, and (x^3)^3 = x^9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-732$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$y = x² + 7x + 11<br>y = x + 3<br><br>The graphs of the equations above intersect at two points. What is the product of the x-coordinates of the intersection points?$q$, $q$["−8","8","11","−6"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Set the expressions equal: x² + 7x + 11 = x + 3, so x² + 6x + 8 = 0. This factors as (x + 4)(x + 2) = 0, so x = −4 or x = −2. The product is 8.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-733$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponential functions$q$, 1, null, $q$The function f(t) = 200(1.03)^t models the number of followers of an account t months after it was first measured. What is the best interpretation of 200 in this context?$q$, $q$["The change in the amount each month","The amount when it was first measured","The amount after 1.03 months","The amount after one month"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$When t = 0, f(0) = 200(1.03)^0 = 200. So 200 is the amount at the time of the first measurement.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-734$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic inequalities$q$, 2, null, $q$How many integer values of x satisfy (x + 4)(x + 1) < 0?$q$, $q$["1","2","4","3"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The product is negative when x is strictly between the roots −4 and −1. The integers −3 through −2 number 2.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-735$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Quadratic equations$q$, 1, null, $q$What are the solutions to the equation 3(x + 8)(x − 9) = 0?$q$, $q$["x = −8 and x = −9","x = 8 and x = −9","x = 8 and x = 9","x = −8 and x = 9"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$A product equals 0 when one of its factors equals 0. Setting (x + 8) = 0 and (x − 9) = 0 gives x = −8 and x = 9.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-736$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Nonlinear systems of equations$q$, 2, null, $q$y = x² + x − 19<br>y = 2x + 1<br><br>The graphs of the equations above intersect at two points. What is the product of the x-coordinates of the intersection points?$q$, $q$["20","−20","−19","1"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Set the expressions equal: x² + x − 19 = 2x + 1, so x² − x − 20 = 0. This factors as (x − 5)(x + 4) = 0, so x = 5 or x = −4. The product is −20.$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-737$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 1, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (4x³)(9x³)?$q$, $q$["13x⁹","13x⁶","36x⁹","36x⁶"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Multiply the coefficients (4 × 9 = 36) and add the exponents of x (3 + 3 = 6).$q$, null),
  ($q$adv-738$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Advanced Math$q$, $q$Equivalent expressions$q$, 2, null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (x − 1)²?$q$, $q$["x² + 1","x² − 2x − 1","x² − x + 1","x² − 2x + 1"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$(p + q)² = p² + 2pq + q². With p = x and q = −1: x² + 2(x)(−1) + (−1)² = x² − 2x + 1.$q$, null),
